# Audio and its derived feature cache: bulky, and the audio is not ours to
# commit. The label database IS committed -- it is the one irreplaceable thing
# here (~23 MB at a full 30-track collection, under 10 MB of git history, so
# plain git handles it; LFS would be all friction and no benefit).
training_data/*.wav
training_data/*.flac
training_data/*.aiff
training_data/*.aif
training_data/*.mp3
training_data/*.ogg
training_data/*.features.npz

# python bytecode from running the tools in place
__pycache__/

# SQLite's WAL sidecars. db.py runs in WAL mode, so until the last connection
# closes, recently written labels may still live in -wal rather than in the
# database file. Never commit these: a -wal committed alongside a database is a
# torn pair, and a database committed without its pending -wal is missing the
# sessions it has not checkpointed yet. Corollary: only commit the database
# when label.py is not running, which is when SQLite has checkpointed and
# removed these.
training_data/*.db-wal
training_data/*.db-shm
